    {
      "question_id": "Q13",
      "question": "What is the difference between split-K and split-Q warp partitioning in FlashAttention-2's comparison?",
      "expected_answerable": true,
      "status": "answered",
      "answer": "Split-K: FlashAttention splits K and V across warps while keeping Q accessible to all warps; each warp computes a slice of QK⊤, then must write intermediate results to shared memory, synchronize, and add them up (requiring inter-warp communication) [S2]. Split-Q (FlashAttention-2): FlashAttention-2 instead splits Q across warps while keeping K and V accessible to all warps; each warp computes its slice of QK⊤ and then multiplies with the shared slice of V to produce its output slice with no inter-warp communication, reducing shared-memory reads/writes and yielding a speedup [S1].",
